// Playwright is not yet configured in this project (no playwright.config.ts,
// no @playwright/test dependency in package.json).
//
// Before this spec can be activated, run:
//   pnpm add -D @playwright/test
//   pnpm exec playwright install
//   # create playwright.config.ts (baseURL, testDir, etc.)
//
// The intended happy-path test (attach library collection to a run → see the
// CoverageBar → open the gap dialog → confirm the protocol rollup) is below.
// Move this file to collection-coverage.spec.ts and fill in the test once
// Playwright is wired up. Component-level coverage already exists in:
//   src/features/screening-assay/components/coverage-bar.test.tsx
//   src/features/screening-assay/components/collection-coverage-chips.test.tsx
//   src/features/screening-assay/components/collection-multi-select.test.tsx
//
// Scenario — Collection coverage on a run, then the protocol rollup:
//
// 1. Attach a library collection to a run.
//    - Open a run-detail page (a run with screened readout data).
//    - In the Collections card, open the CollectionMultiSelect picker; the
//      library-typed collections sort first. Select a library collection
//      (e.g. "Kinase Set") and confirm the attach.
//    - Assert a CoverageBar renders for that collection showing
//      `covered / total · pct%` (e.g. "1,840 / 2,000 · 92%").
//
// 2. Inspect the unscreened gap.
//    - The CoverageBar shows an "N remaining" affordance (e.g. "160 remaining")
//      when total > covered. Click it.
//    - Assert the CoverageGapDialog opens and lists the unscreened molecules
//      (those in the collection with no readout data on this run).
//
// 3. Confirm the protocol-level rollup.
//    - Navigate to the protocol that owns the run.
//    - Assert the "Library coverage" rollup shows the cumulative coverage % for
//      that collection with the "across N runs" subtitle (e.g. "across 3 runs"),
//      reflecting the union of all the protocol's runs that attach it.
